**Dependencies:**

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
  <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-cache</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.github.ben-manes.caffeine</groupId>
  <artifactId>caffeine</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

**Enable caching** + programmatic Caffeine config (recommended over `application.yml` for fine control):

```java
@Configuration
@EnableCaching
public class CacheConfig {

    @Bean
    public CacheManager cacheManager() {
        CaffeineCacheManager mgr = new CaffeineCacheManager(
            "products", "userProfiles", "featureFlags");
        mgr.setCaffeine(Caffeine.newBuilder()
            .maximumSize(10_000)
            .expireAfterWrite(Duration.ofMinutes(10))
            .refreshAfterWrite(Duration.ofMinutes(2))
            .recordStats());
        return mgr;
    }
}
```

**Per-cache custom config** (different sizes/TTLs per cache):

```java
@Bean
public CacheManager cacheManager() {
    SimpleCacheManager mgr = new SimpleCacheManager();
    mgr.setCaches(List.of(
        caffeineCache("products", 50_000, Duration.ofMinutes(30)),
        caffeineCache("featureFlags", 1_000, Duration.ofMinutes(5)),
        caffeineCache("userProfiles", 10_000, Duration.ofMinutes(15))
    ));
    return mgr;
}

private CaffeineCache caffeineCache(String name, long size, Duration ttl) {
    return new CaffeineCache(name,
        Caffeine.newBuilder()
            .maximumSize(size)
            .expireAfterWrite(ttl)
            .recordStats()
            .build());
}
```

**Usage with `@Cacheable`:**

```java
@Service
public class ProductService {

    @Cacheable(value = "products", key = "#id", sync = true)
    public Product findById(String id) {
        return repo.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    }

    @CacheEvict(value = "products", key = "#p.id")
    public void update(Product p) { repo.save(p); }
}
```

`sync = true` is important: it prevents thundering herd by coalescing concurrent requests for the same key.

**Async refresh pattern** — hot data stays fresh without blocking reads:

```java
LoadingCache<String, Product> cache = Caffeine.newBuilder()
    .maximumSize(10_000)
    .expireAfterWrite(Duration.ofMinutes(10))
    .refreshAfterWrite(Duration.ofMinutes(2))
    .recordStats()
    .build(key -> repo.findById(key).orElseThrow());
```

After 2 minutes, next read triggers async reload; old value still served until new value is ready.

**Async loading** for I/O-bound loaders:

```java
AsyncLoadingCache<String, Product> cache = Caffeine.newBuilder()
    .maximumSize(10_000)
    .expireAfterWrite(Duration.ofMinutes(10))
    .buildAsync((key, exec) ->
        CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> loadFromRemote(key), exec));
```

**Enable stats:**

```java
Caffeine.newBuilder()
    .maximumSize(10_000)
    .expireAfterWrite(Duration.ofMinutes(10))
    .recordStats();
```

**Expose to Micrometer:**

```java
@Bean
public MeterBinder cacheMetrics(CacheManager cm) {
    return registry -> {
        for (String name : cm.getCacheNames()) {
            Cache<Object, Object> native = ((CaffeineCache) cm.getCache(name))
                .getNativeCache();
            CaffeineCacheMetrics.monitor(registry, native, name);
        }
    };
}
```

**Key metrics:**
- `cache.size` — current entries
- `cache.gets` — total gets (hit + miss)
- `cache.puts` — total puts
- `cache.evictions` — evicted entries (size / expiry)
- `cache.hit.ratio` — derived (`hits / (hits + misses)`)
- `cache.load.duration` — load latency from `CacheLoader`
- `cache.load.failure` — loader exceptions

**Grafana alerts to set:**
- Hit ratio drops below 80% (cache not doing its job)
- Eviction rate spikes (too small or load burst)
- Load duration > threshold (source slow)
- Load failure rate > 0 (errors propagating)

**Access stats programmatically:**

```java
CacheStats stats = cache.stats();
log.info("hit ratio: {}%, avg load: {}ms, evictions: {}",
    stats.hitRate() * 100,
    stats.averageLoadPenalty() / 1_000_000,
    stats.evictionCount());
```

**Actuator endpoint** (`/actuator/caches`) exposes cache names, statistics with Spring Boot 2.1+.
